h actor's identity, weapon ownership, geography and accumulated damage. Physical chain for every exchange: anticipation, ground-supported propulsion through legs and hips, trajectory, visible contact or evasion, momentum transfer, displacement, reaction, recovery. A block redirects momentum; a miss carries inertia. Balance, friction, traction, gravity and center of mass govern motion. Reactions caused by impacts start after contact; anticipatory defenses remain allowed. Feet step, pivot, skid or drag visibly, never slide rigidly. Grapples require grip, tension and leverage; jumps require compression, takeoff, ballistic travel and landing. Cloth, hair and loose material follow bodies with delayed secondary motion; environmental response follows the impact. Keep attack lines, contact and body displacement readable in the requested camera. Continue motion between actions without automatic guard resets, freeze poses, teleporting, limb fusion or interpenetration. No artificial slow motion or speed ramps unless requested. No flashes, cuts or camera shake to conceal missing contact. Finish requested attacks before any subsequent dialogue, preserving the exact dialogue and requested audio. Do not invent extra opponents, injuries, dialogue or soundtracks. Follow the requested intensity and the character's established abilities.",
